https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.1.tar.xz
SHA-256 cf38e0e28c7e5605942c4a77755349b0145804a397af37eb1fb4c77cb237f635

Preferred editable source: clean-english-v2.txt and generate-clean-english-v2.py,
with the pinned upstream engine/data and tool identities in clean-english-v2.json.
Install development-only eSpeak NG 1.52.0 and FFmpeg 9.0.1; neither is linked into
or required by the Cueglint application. Run:
  python3 parity/fixtures/generate-clean-english-v2.py NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY
The output directory must not exist. The script checks versions and voice data,
writes audio to files only, validates mono PCM16 format and records hashes.
It fixes en-us/145 words per minute/pitch 50/amplitude 100/gap 0/-D deterministic
randomness, then SWR resamples to 16 kHz with no dithering and bitexact flags.
No audio is played, no person is recorded, and no voice/speed is selected by ASR
performance. This is a different acoustic fixture from retired Samantha v1.
